<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-104476 size-full" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/18-LEGO-Icons-11375-Ferrari-F2004-Michael-Schumacher-March-2026-Release-Date-Lifestyle-3.jpg" alt="" width="1116" height="734" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/18-LEGO-Icons-11375-Ferrari-F2004-Michael-Schumacher-March-2026-Release-Date-Lifestyle-3.jpg 1116w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/18-LEGO-Icons-11375-Ferrari-F2004-Michael-Schumacher-March-2026-Release-Date-Lifestyle-3-300x197.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/18-LEGO-Icons-11375-Ferrari-F2004-Michael-Schumacher-March-2026-Release-Date-Lifestyle-3-1024x673.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/18-LEGO-Icons-11375-Ferrari-F2004-Michael-Schumacher-March-2026-Release-Date-Lifestyle-3-768x505.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1116px) 100vw, 1116px" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Where are my car lovers at? I’ve got a LEGO Icon set for you, and this one is special-it hits close to the heart. This is because it features a Michael Schumacher minifigure. And for those who don’t know him, Michael is one of the greatest drivers in motorsport history, bagging 7 Formula One World Drivers’ Championships–something I can only imagine on my end.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The set has 735 pieces, which is fine by me. So, if you are not looking for something especially large, this set fits right in. You’ll get a faithful replica of the red Ferrari that graced the tracks in the 2004 season. Even the V10 engine adds to the authentic detailing, which includes a working steering wheel and slick tires.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You’ll also get a display stand with the original vehicle’s specs. Still, I think the best part of owning this set is the quote from the seven-time world champion.</span></p>
