<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-90062 alignright" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/18-LEGO-Icons-10338-Bumblebee-Transformers-July-2024-Set-Images-300x249.jpg" alt="" width="320" height="265" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/18-LEGO-Icons-10338-Bumblebee-Transformers-July-2024-Set-Images-300x249.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/18-LEGO-Icons-10338-Bumblebee-Transformers-July-2024-Set-Images-1024x849.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/18-LEGO-Icons-10338-Bumblebee-Transformers-July-2024-Set-Images-768x637.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/18-LEGO-Icons-10338-Bumblebee-Transformers-July-2024-Set-Images.jpg 1110w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px" /></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">I know some people would rather go for something more than just having a car on their shelf or table. Well, a Creator 3-in-1 set would do the job, but I have something even better. How about a robot that transforms into a car?</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The Bumblebee set is one of the fun models you can get as an adult. It has 950 pieces, meaning you’ll get a sizable challenge assembling them. The set also has articulating joints, allowing you to pose it.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">I’d be careful with the backpack if I were you because of the ion blaster and a jetpack. And when you are ready to display it, you’ll find the display plaque particularly helpful in listing the Autobot’s power statistics.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Sets like this typically belong to the Technic category. But I guess Bumblebee has attained a legendary status, something most movie lovers will agree with. Note that there is a much bigger sibling, the Transformers: Soundwave set, but that is above our budget for today.</span></p>
